NAME
       namei - follow a path name one part at a time

SYNOPSIS
       namei [-l] [-m] [-o] PATH...

DESCRIPTION
       namei splits PATH into its parts and shows each one on its own line,
       from / down to the last name, following symbolic links. With -l it
       shows the permissions and owner of every directory on the way. That
       makes it the quickest way to find out why a user cannot reach a file:
       one directory without the x permission anywhere on the path blocks
       access.

OPTIONS
       -l, --long
              Show the permissions, owner and group (the same as -m -o).

       -m, --modes
              Show the permissions.

       -o, --owners
              Show the owner and group.

EXAMPLES
           namei -l /home/student/public_html/index.html

SEE ALSO
       ls(1), stat(1), readlink(1), realpath(1)
